      "id": "ln42pqt",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8.1 Meaning of Operating System"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "An Operating System serves as a bridge between the user and computer hardware.",
        "Primary functions of an OS include process management, memory allocation, device control, and file management.",
        "Batch operating systems group similar jobs together, whereas time-sharing systems allocate CPU time slots to multiple users.",
        "Multiprocessing operating systems utilize two or more CPUs to enhance execution speed and system reliability.",
        "Windows OS relies on a Graphical User Interface (GUI) with core elements like the Taskbar, Desktop, and File Explorer."
      ],
      "id": "emo9sw0"
    },
